{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Declared mutants of the passes' names, debug groups, CPU times and the frames' GPU time (render-pipeline declaration section 15, v8-arch-gyo2-render-a3; 判定 T1 to T4). One per independently wrong decision (tests/common/mutation/README.md, criteria 1 to 3 and 9). The batch changes no Design Invariant (A3 is a lower-tier batch), so every guard is a 判定 of section 15. tm-label-* and tm-timing-* need no GPU (label cpu); the other tm-* need a GPU (label gpu, sdl_gpu.timing); tm-submit-not-tracked and tm-status-timing-not-given run sdl_gpu.frames, which shows a window (not run by the A3 card: L1 runs the case, not the mutants). Not added (with the reason): the frame's timing not rebuilt from its commands (RecordPasses then indexes past the timings: undefined behaviour, a crash, not an assertion); a fence taken as done before it is signaled (Capture waits for its fence before looking, so no case without a window tells it apart); the fences let go at the device's end (a leak, not seen from outside); Submit looking at the fences before the swapchain's wait (the bound only gets looser, by the wait: not seen from outside); the debug group's name in a capture tool (CI has no capture tool: only the count is checked, 15.4).",
  "mutants": [
    {
      "id": "tm-label-no-index",
      "what": "15.3 (1): a pass's name leaves out its place, so two passes alike share a name",
      "guards": [
        "render-pipeline-declaration 15 判定 T1"
      ],
      "file": "plugins/sdl_gpu/src/PassLabels.hpp",
      "find": "    std::string label = \"#\" + std::to_string(index) + \" \";",
      "replace": "    std::string label = \"#0 \";",
      "target": "gyo_sdl_gpu_tests",
      "cases": "sdl_gpu pass labels:*",
      "expect": "\\[tm\\-names\\-distinct\\]"
    },
    {
      "id": "tm-label-target-ignored",
      "what": "15.3 (1): a pass's name says main whatever its target",
      "guards": [
        "render-pipeline-declaration 15 判定 T1"
      ],
      "file": "plugins/sdl_gpu/src/PassLabels.hpp",
      "find": "    label += target ? \" -> target \" + std::to_string(target->value) : std::string(\" -> main\");",
      "replace": "    label += std::string(\" -> main\");",
      "target": "gyo_sdl_gpu_tests",
      "cases": "sdl_gpu pass labels:*",
      "expect": "\\[tm\\-names\\-target\\]"
    },
    {
      "id": "tm-label-shader-dropped",
      "what": "15.3 (1): a full-screen pass's name leaves out its shader",
      "guards": [
        "render-pipeline-declaration 15 判定 T1"
      ],
      "file": "plugins/sdl_gpu/src/PassLabels.hpp",
      "find": "            if constexpr (std::is_same_v<Pass, R::PassFullscreen>) return \"PassFullscreen \" + p.shader;",
      "replace": "            if constexpr (std::is_same_v<Pass, R::PassFullscreen>) return \"PassFullscreen\";",
      "target": "gyo_sdl_gpu_tests",
      "cases": "sdl_gpu pass labels:*",
      "expect": "\\[tm\\-names\\-shader\\]"
    },
    {
      "id": "tm-label-kind-wrong",
      "what": "15.3 (1): a pass's name gives another kind than its own (a depth-only pass named as a 3D one)",
      "guards": [
        "render-pipeline-declaration 15 判定 T1"
      ],
      "file": "plugins/sdl_gpu/src/PassLabels.hpp",
      "find": "            if constexpr (std::is_same_v<Pass, R::PassDepth>) return \"PassDepth\";",
      "replace": "            if constexpr (std::is_same_v<Pass, R::PassDepth>) return \"Pass3D\";",
      "target": "gyo_sdl_gpu_tests",
      "cases": "sdl_gpu pass labels:*",
      "expect": "\\[tm\\-names\\-kind\\]"
    },
    {
      "id": "tm-timing-not-named",
      "what": "15.3 (1): a frame's timings are not named by PassLabel",
      "guards": [
        "render-pipeline-declaration 15 判定 T1"
      ],
      "file": "plugins/sdl_gpu/src/PassLabels.hpp",
      "find": "    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < commands.passes.size(); ++i) timing.passes.push_back(PassTiming{PassLabel(commands.passes[i], i)});",
      "replace": "    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < commands.passes.size(); ++i) timing.passes.push_back(PassTiming{});",
      "target": "gyo_sdl_gpu_tests",
      "cases": "sdl_gpu pass labels:*",
      "expect": "\\[tm\\-timing\\-named\\]"
    },
    {
      "id": "tm-timing-starts-recorded",
      "what": "15.3 (3): a frame's timings start as recorded (before the adapter records anything)",
      "guards": [
        "render-pipeline-declaration 15 判定 T1"
      ],
      "file": "plugins/sdl_gpu/src/PassLabels.hpp",
      "find": "    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < commands.passes.size(); ++i) timing.passes.push_back(PassTiming{PassLabel(commands.passes[i], i)});",
      "replace": "    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < commands.passes.size(); ++i) timing.passes.push_back(PassTiming{PassLabel(commands.passes[i], i), true});",
      "target": "gyo_sdl_gpu_tests",
      "cases": "sdl_gpu pass labels:*",
      "expect": "\\[tm\\-timing\\-unrecorded\\]"
    },
    {
      "id": "tm-frames-not-counted",
